 ## Background
-Procedural terrain generation using noise functions has been a staple in computer graphics and game development for decades. The specific implementation described here, using FBM and OpenSimplex2 noise, is commonly found in indie voxel engine tutorials and open-source projects [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, unofficial]. The use of image sampling for terrain generation is a technique employed in WebGL-based voxel engines to allow for artist-defined landscapes [S3, unofficial]. The cliffs layer and smooth terrain grid variants represent more specialized approaches to terrain generation, focusing on specific aesthetic or structural requirements [S4, S5, unofficial].
